[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40739"] :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]},\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an **orthonormal** basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|a|+|b|+|c|?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis:\n\n- ${u}_{1}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- ${u}_{2}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, $B={{u}_{1},{u}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthonormal basis of $V.$\n\nFinally, $a=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},$ $b=0,$ $c=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c|=|-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|+|\\,0\\,|+|\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-41035"] :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{c}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{5\\cdot 4+5\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $c=-4,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{a}=\\frac{-4}{1}=-4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-86850/selection/12dbc69044704dfa22a8053218d682009f2daafd75e482a353d857f0332a4216" :answer/id #uuid "e5308b4f-3612-5103-9346-5aeb29ca39f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86850/selection/b5672e3d5d727bcb709f33eeb0f8df47c72e1fe5fb135d6d9ea4ceefea5f0aa1" :answer/id #uuid "25b6112e-d9c7-5330-ad5f-ab6f7c733076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86850/selection/a4cba348147fb76b37f899b2adb5ac164f412a12fe4a7f46fba75da282025c81" :answer/id #uuid "5c888d00-5c35-539c-a93f-9a5fafb946cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86850/selection/34219f229a95b374101226ed6e8380124ab0bbcf04f479caa9d1b203ca15969e" :answer/id #uuid "5dc6f8a0-0f05-5037-99d5-ce080dabb761" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86850/selection/ae94b17d9a4c31cb8b8b32b5e855bebc16aaa6d99f564985973e8ff02dca8b49" :answer/id #uuid "ffadd238-d345-5c9b-8a56-6fb9959abf66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86850/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4accb12-60f8-595c-9266-8a13f681fc3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86850/selection/ae94b17d9a4c31cb8b8b32b5e855bebc16aaa6d99f564985973e8ff02dca8b49" :answer-field/choices ["q-86850/selection/12dbc69044704dfa22a8053218d682009f2daafd75e482a353d857f0332a4216" "q-86850/selection/b5672e3d5d727bcb709f33eeb0f8df47c72e1fe5fb135d6d9ea4ceefea5f0aa1" "q-86850/selection/a4cba348147fb76b37f899b2adb5ac164f412a12fe4a7f46fba75da282025c81" "q-86850/selection/34219f229a95b374101226ed6e8380124ab0bbcf04f479caa9d1b203ca15969e" "q-86850/selection/ae94b17d9a4c31cb8b8b32b5e855bebc16aaa6d99f564985973e8ff02dca8b49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86850" :question/id #uuid "36c3eb21-9ecf-5719-be65-00aec9bbb34c" :question/math-academy-id "q-86850" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{c}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$ \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{0\\cdot \\sqrt{2}+(-5)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-3)}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{13}{3} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{13}{3} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $b=-\\frac{13}{3},$ $c=-1,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{b}=\\frac{-1}{(-\\frac{13}{3})}=\\frac{3}{13}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-86850/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b15719b6-0ce4-5fb8-80be-abcaf9344a10"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86850"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86854/selection/12c947543f46d7f79577370c4389a4cae90ebf066ce8bf9c5d99e707825b4968" :answer/id #uuid "1f5496c6-b4f8-574f-9f9b-b9eeb45a2b9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86854/selection/181d1f839d214e5807f4235aba03fc371467f433c702fbf48b29ccfdaa41b68d" :answer/id #uuid "1e5d44d7-4b60-5339-b10f-ef4df2293796" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86854/selection/b2063ac39ffa6fbe721c72ca256ec7466f6b97b0165c7b0f39ff0b7cf53d2968" :answer/id #uuid "9376245a-11f6-5724-9939-b6cae9ef5c4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86854/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "00df12d0-5301-5e79-bb0e-92e3d1cce05d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86854/selection/5dedd3fc97eb64beda5d906ad6dd87aaae34db54c1ed35ec3a4b810f0ed5b6e3" :answer/id #uuid "fde3a84f-bed4-5b48-b38b-ccf645358a2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86854/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b5fd301-39f3-5c20-9d23-dacc79cc7677" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86854/selection/b2063ac39ffa6fbe721c72ca256ec7466f6b97b0165c7b0f39ff0b7cf53d2968" :answer-field/choices ["q-86854/s